AWS-005 — Workflow Execution

Document ID: AWS-005
Title: Workflow Execution
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Workflow Execution Model (CWEM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Workflow Execution Model establishes the normative process by which Canonical Workflow Definitions are instantiated, executed, monitored, coordinated, and completed while preserving engineering intent, governance, determinism, and traceability.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Execution architecture
Workflow instantiation
Execution context
Activity execution
State management
Event generation
Failure handling
Completion semantics

This specification applies to every Workflow Instance.

3. Canonical Definition

Workflow Execution is the governed realization of a Canonical Workflow Definition within a specific execution context, producing a Workflow Instance that records the complete operational history of the workflow.

Execution realizes a workflow.

It SHALL NOT modify the workflow definition.

4. Objectives

The Workflow Execution Model SHALL:

Execute workflows deterministically.
Preserve engineering intent.
Maintain governance.
Coordinate participants.
Generate traceable execution history.
Support recovery.
Enable monitoring.
Preserve reproducibility.
5. Execution Principles

Every workflow execution SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Definition Integrity

Workflow Definitions SHALL remain immutable during execution.

Instance Isolation

Each Workflow Instance SHALL execute independently of other instances unless explicitly synchronized.

Deterministic Behavior

Equivalent workflow definitions, execution contexts, and inputs SHALL produce equivalent execution behavior unless adaptive execution is explicitly authorized.

Governance Enforcement

Applicable Canonical Policy Objects SHALL govern execution throughout the workflow lifecycle.

Traceability

Every execution activity SHALL generate an auditable execution history.

Recoverability

Execution SHALL support governed recovery following interruption or failure.

